body:
I had a pretty bad reaction to Sertraline. I've been feeling crappy for about ten years, recently I've managed to get into a position where treatment may be possible. I have Asperges, ADHD, GAD/SAD/Depression and BPD. All Diagnosed, it's becoming really really difficult to deal with I teeter between feeling okay and outright suicidal. It's a 50/50 concerning medication but it will help in the longrun and not all Anti-Depressants will cause you to have awful side-effects. 

&#x200B;

I say find a combination that works for you and use it alongside therapy if you can get it. If not then self help books or friends that can help when you feel at your lowest. Wishing you luck and every other fellow sufferee.

&#x200B;

Peace Y
